#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115228 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115058 :question/id #uuid "7ab158e6-4222-5cab-88a0-85ce74a7d4b2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4413" :question/problem "Given that $A, B,$ and $C$ are $6 \\times 6$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nI. $A(BC) = (AB)C$\n\nII. $A(B+C) = BA+CA$\n\nIII. $A(B+C) = AB+AC$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C = A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+C) = AB + AC$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\nAB + AC  \\neq BA + CA.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C = AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C) = AB+AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545182 :question-generator/id #uuid "227b6b15-7345-547c-a312-6f2320ca1a08" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186115228.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1067aa3d-2b51-5b1a-b638-8cd254e921c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448632} {:answer/id #uuid "a3967aa3-4b50-5c5c-b5fe-aa477f5fe032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1067aa3d-2b51-5b1a-b638-8cd254e921c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448632} :answer-field/id #uuid "149d811f-1bfd-59da-848a-31d1c4100def" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449356} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id 